  "description": "A trusty steed for the gravel curious road riders among us. On road or off, the Provincial Road 2’s stability-focused steel frame is flickable and responsive. From tarmac focused group rides, to cyclocross and bikepacking, this bike is up for it. Like past Provincials, the Road 2 has impressive tire clearance, making it a great choice for touring on less than stellar terrain. The carbon fork uses a 12mm thru-axle instead of a standard QR set up, to reduce flex under hard braking, cornering, and accelerating. A wide and supportive Fizik Terra saddle keeps you comfortable during those long rides. SRAM’s gravel focused 12-speed Apex groupset, offers tons of mechanical advantage to help flatten out the climbs. By moving to a 1x12 drivetrain, we have removed a potential point of failure in the front, the derailleur, giving you the durability enjoyed by mountain bikers for years. No matter the terrain or the grade, the powerful hydraulic disc brakes let you keep your speed right where you want it.\n\nDesigned to be as fun to ride on your daily commute as it is out bikepacking, the versatile Provincial line is great bang for your buck\n\nReynolds 520 chromoly steel frame with lowered bottom bracket for stable handling\n\nCarbon fibre fork with aluminum steerer lower the weight of the bike while improving comfort\n\nFront fork designed for use with 12mm thru axles\n\nFrame is equipped with eyelets for fenders, a rear rack, and 3 bottle cages for those long adventures\n\nFrame and fork have plenty of clearance, allowing for tires that measure up to 45mm in width\n\nSRAM Apex 1x12 gruppo yields fast shifts and solid braking in a lightweight package\n\nDoubleTap system, shifting up or down is done with a with short sweep of your fingers\n\nSRAM Apex hydraulic disc brakes provide outstanding power and modulation regardless of weather\n\nSRAM Centerline 160mm rotors provide plenty of stopping power\n\nSRAM Apex 1 crankset uses X-Sync™ chainring technology for excellent chain retention in rough terrain\n\nFormula hubs use sealed cartridge bearings for smoothness and durability\n\nEaston EA50 bars features a 16° flare for a comfortable and stable position on rough roads\n\nVittoria Terreno Dry tires are 40mm wide to soak up road and trail vibration\n\nMEC carbon fibre seat post helps soak up vibration\n\nFizik Terra Alpaca X5 is 145mm wide, comfortably cradling your sit bones on rough terrain and long rides\n\nPart of MEC’s Provincial collection – a versatile series of bags and bikes that are just as useful on your commute, as they are on your gravel grinds and bikepacking adventures\n\nBikes are covered by MEC's Rocksolid Guarantee and Bike Service Agreement. You can bring your bike to any MEC bike shop for free adjustments and minor maintenance for a year after purchase\n\nMEC bikes are designed in Canada. Everything from the frames to the graphics are developed at the MEC Head Office in Vancouver, BC",
